w24-alert-silence-is-not-fix: credit and licence

This folder is a clean-room method sketch inspired by:

  Zhezhen Cao, Weiyuan Ding, Bowen Xu.
  "Preserve the Vulnerability, Break the Alert: Testing the Robustness of
  CodeQL Taint Tracking with Natural Rewrites". arXiv:2611.17123 v1,
  submitted 12 Nov 2026. https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.17123

Paper licence: arXiv.org perpetual, non-exclusive license 1.0
(http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/), as linked on the abs
page. That licence grants arXiv the right to distribute the paper and grants
no reuse to anyone else, so nothing of the paper's text is reproduced here
beyond seven short abstract sentences quoted, for attribution, in
paper_evidence.json.

Clean-room statement: only the abstract was read. The PDF was not read. No
code, rewrite, prompt, flow, benchmark, analyzer model or data of the paper
is used; the abstract links none. CodeQL is not used, ported or modelled,
no language model is used, and there is no multi-analyzer comparison. The
toy taint analyzer, its one modelling gap, the executor, the fixtures and
all code here are this sketch's own, written from the idea that a
disappearing alert is weak evidence of a fix. No human data is used.

The authors' figures appear only in paper_evidence.json, quoted verbatim,
marked UNVERIFIED and on_unmeasured.
